One <110> dumbbell in a bcc crystal: the introductory example.

  sh insert.sh     builds an 8 x 8 x 8 bcc cell (1024 atoms) and inserts the
                   dumbbell at site (1,1,1): 1025 atoms in formd_new.str
  sh clean.sh      removes the files produced by the run

To change the cell, the sites or the defect type, edit the three short blocks
of insert.sh. Keep the lattice parameter at 2.8553.

The other files are the result converted to other formats (POSCAR, xyz,
LAMMPS, CFG, gin), kept as illustrations.
